# Format: ENV_NAME|folder|item|field
# Render these to a local .env file before deploy; never commit rendered values.
#
# Persistent Diary/Goals store on the shared critical Postgres service.
# After the `critical-internal` Docker network and `postgres` alias exist, update
# only the host component of this Vaultwarden field from the old raw bridge IP to
# `postgres`; preserve username/password/port/database/TLS parameters.
PERSONAL_DASHBOARD_DATABASE_URL|homelab|personal-dashboard/database|database_url
#
# No committed secret values are required for the MVP default reverse-proxy-auth deployment.
# Non-secret live-render inputs can be copied from .env.example.
#
# If Ben later chooses app-level shared-password auth, create items such as:
# DASHBOARD_SHARED_PASSWORD|homelab|personal-dashboard/auth|shared-password
# DASHBOARD_SESSION_SECRET|homelab|personal-dashboard/auth|session-secret
#
# If Cloudflare public-hostname/DNS changes are automated instead of done in the
# Zero Trust dashboard, use this existing/expected API item and keep values local:
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN|homelab|cloudflare/api|api_token
# CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_ID|homelab|cloudflare/api|zone_id
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID|homelab|cloudflare/api|account_id
#
# Investment Screener staged provider-fallback keys (optional, fail-closed).
# Adapters are disabled unless their env var is present at runtime. Values are
# never committed; store them in the Vaultwarden `Homelab` folder.
# Current actual FMP item verified by the Kanban unblock path; folder names are case-sensitive in bw:
# FMP_API_KEY|Homelab|FMP_API_KEY|password
# EODHD fundamentals feed (multi-market; folder Homelab, LOGIN item -> login.password):
# EODHD_API_KEY|Homelab|EODHD_API_KEY|password
# Preferred normalized future FMP item:
# FMP_API_KEY|Homelab|investment-screener/fmp|api_key
# ALPHA_VANTAGE_API_KEY|Homelab|investment-screener/alpha-vantage|api_key
